{"author":{"id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMTA5NDkz","is_bot":false,"login":"td72","name":"Kohei Hosokawa"},"body":"## Motivation\n\nThe issue and PR lists show open items only (`gh issue list` / `gh pr list` defaults). Looking at what was just closed or merged means leaving vig.\n\n## Spec\n\n1. **`x`** on the GitHub page toggles the issue and PR lists between open and all (`--state all`, same `--limit`); closed / merged items render dimmed with a state marker (`✓` merged, `✗` closed, `○` open).\n2. Both states are plain `gh` list calls (no GraphQL points) and are cached per state; the #177 change check (already `state=all`) refreshes whichever is shown.\n3. **`github-show-closed \"on\" | \"off\"`** (default `off`) sets the initial state; the header shows `closed` while they are included.\n4. Docs (guide GitHub chapter, Config Reference en / ja, README), demo tape, fixtures re-recorded with the `--state all` lists.\n","comments":[],"createdAt":"2026-09-10T05:39:06Z","labels":[{"id":"LA_kwDORNPWJs8AAAACXrzvTg","name":"enhancement","description":"New feature or request","color":"a2eeef"}],"number":186,"state":"OPEN","title":"GitHub: toggle closed issues / PRs in the lists"}
